Fri Aug  8 14:03:25 PDT 1980

The binaries in the ucb directory seem to have been compiled at a time
when a bug existed on the cory system in getpwent.  As a result, if you
aren't running the Cory hashed password stuff, all programs which try
to look in the password file will fail.  These programs include whoami,
the -l option to ls, and so on.  If you recompile on your own system
the problem will go away.

Tue Jan 13 21:44:20 PST 1981

Some of the binaries in this directory are missing or out of date,
due to the fact that 2bsd is distributed from a vax and not all
pdp-11 binaries are conveniently available.  The ex/vi and csh
binaries are promised to be up to date for both v6 and v7.  It
is probably a good idea to recompile everything you want.
